WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:01.967
DAVID TAYLOR GOMES:
<i> Students in high school,</i>

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.669
<i> there's this feeling
 of suffocation,</i>

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.438
<i> of everyone trying to tell you</i>

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.239
you have to be
the absolute best.

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:08.374
♪ (TENSE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.743
KYLE HOLMES:
<i> Students truly believe
 that their class rank</i>

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:14.147
and where they go to college
is gonna determine everything.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.015
STUDENT:
<i> A 4.0 isn't enough anymore,</i>

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:17.584
<i> which is funny 'cause
 that used to be perfect.</i>

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.619
But now, it's all about
being better than perfect.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:25.057
<i> ♪ What the hell, what the hell
 Is going on here? ♪</i>

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:28.594
HOLMES:
<i> In writing the musical</i> Ranked,
<i> we wanted to amplify</i>

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:30.496
everything our students
were saying to us.

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:33.099
There's a huge pressure
to keep up GPA

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.701
<i> while balancing drama
 and being on a sports team</i>

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.637
and the National Honor Society.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.039
HOLMES:
<i> At a school like Granite Bay,</i>

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:41.908
<i> everyone knows
 where everyone is rank-wise.</i>

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.210
<i> Technology has made it
 so prevalent.</i>

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.213
Kids are oftentimes
finding themselves
very miserable.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:51.751
<i> ♪ When does this feeling
 Go away? ♪</i>

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.920
<i> ♪ This tightness in my chest ♪</i>

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:55.454
SPEAKER:
<i> Most parents don't know.</i>

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:58.258
<i> I think this show
 started conversations.</i>

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:01.627
GOMES:<i> We had
 schools all over the country
 reaching out to us,</i>

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:03.195
<i> wanting to license
 and perform the show.</i>

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:06.933
<i>From California to West Virginia
 to New York.</i>

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.568
HOLMES:<i> Saying, "Hey, these are
 our kids' stories too,"</i>

00:01:09.668 --> 00:01:11.971
<i> and "How can we work with you
 to tell that?"</i>

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:13.472
GOMES:<i> But then...</i>

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.408
ANNOUNCER: (OVER PA)
<i> School will be closed</i>

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:18.711
<i> in response to
 the COVID-19 virus.</i>

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.012
SPEAKER 2:<i> For a lot of kids,</i>

00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:23.349
<i> theater is where they find
 the place where they belong.</i>

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:26.352
<i> Can't do theater very well
 with a mask on your face.</i>

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:29.155
HOLMES:<i> And then we realized
 there was no reason</i>

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.390
Ranked<i> couldn't be adapted
 online.</i>

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.727
SPEAKER 3:<i> The arts is our glue
 during this pandemic.</i>

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.799
<i> ♪ I'm gonna come up for air ♪</i>

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.801
<i> ♪ I can't keep pretending ♪</i>

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.338
For our communities,
education is your key
to success.

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:51.210
SPEAKER 3:
<i> College represents a way
 to raise their economic state.</i>

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.946
<i> ♪ Happy endings have a cost ♪</i>

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:57.249
SPEAKER 4:<i> Opportunities
 are not evenly given out
 in this world.</i>

00:01:57.816 --> 00:01:59.651
SPEAKER 5:<i> Our students
 are growing up where</i>

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.388
<i> they're experiencing racism,
 oppression.</i>

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:06.225
SPEAKER 6:<i> It's scary to see
 how the world really is.</i>

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:10.496
<i> ♪ Why do I always feel
 so forgotten? ♪</i>

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:12.331
STUDENT 2:<i> I can't let
 the pressure stop me.</i>

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:13.733
<i>I still have to live my dreams.</i>

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.134
<i> ♪ Just breathe ♪</i>

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.270
STUDENT 3:<i> Theater,
 it gives me hope.</i>

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.976
GOMES:<i> I think this show
 is a bit of a wake-up call.</i>

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:27.480
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES, CONCLUDES) ♪

